  "id": "COMPOUND:29801 - PROTEIN:710",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between (2R)-pentan-2-ol and ATP-binding cassette sub-family A member 1 (ABCA1) through multiple indirect pathways. The compound (2R)-pentan-2-ol is identified as a target of several molecules, including Cis-Bis(Methylthio)Silvatin and (3beta,5alpha,7alpha)-3,7-Dihydroxyandrostan-17-one, which in turn target ABCA1. Additionally, (2R)-pentan-2-ol is also a target of Myosin light chain kinase 3, which is itself a target of a complex molecule that also targets ABCA1. These findings collectively indicate that (2R)-pentan-2-ol may influence ABCA1 through a series of molecular interactions, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence is supported by multiple high-scoring pathways, suggesting a plausible but not fully elucidated relationship. The strength of the evidence is moderate, and further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct interaction between (2R)-pentan-2-ol and ABCA1.",
